\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each connected closed smooth Riemannian surface (M,g), does one finite C(M,g) bound $H^{1}_g({u=0})\leq C(M,g)\surd \lambda $ for every nonzero real smooth eigenfunction $-\Delta _g$ $u=\lambda u$ with $\lambda >0$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each connected closed smooth Riemannian surface (M,g), does one finite C(M,g) bound $H^{1}_g({u=0})\leq C(M,g)\surd \lambda $ for every nonzero real smooth eigenfunction $-\Delta _g$ $u=\lambda u$ with $\lambda >0$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://archive.intlpress.com/site/pub/files/_fulltext/journals/cdm/2018/2018/0001/CDM-2018-2018-0001-a004.pdf}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Sharp-nodal-length-on-smooth-surfaces-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

